text:
The system/internal sorting was easy. The sort order for directories would require too much configuration in `.clang-format`, and I decided it wasn't worth the effort.

We want this:
```#include &lt;bitcoin/system/constants.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;bitcoin/system/constraints.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;bitcoin/system/chain/block.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;bitcoin/system/chain/chain.hpp&gt;```
But .clang-format would do the following because chain comes before constants.

```#include &lt;bitcoin/system/chain/block.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;bitcoin/system/chain/chain.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;bitcoin/system/constants.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;bitcoin/system/constraints.hpp&gt;```
We can make it work, but we'd have to paste tonnes of directory paths into .clang-format and give them priorities. It'll just be another shit to maintain. We just trust our eyeballs sorting for now.
